ment in the before/after display, even on different screen sizes. I\'ll adapt this exact CSS-based image cropping method, as it\'s been proven effective.\n\n\n**Refining Image Rendering**\n\nI\'m now integrating real `<img>` tags for the image display! I\'ve confirmed that the \"After\" image will be rendered directly with `object-cover` and `w-full h-full`. The \"Before\" image within a cropped container using a similar method, matching the previous coding pattern perfectly. Next, I\'ll review `BeforeAfter.tsx` to ensure smooth integration, then design selection buttons for the menu. I\'ll consider tab menus, thumbnails, and styled badges. I\'ve got two project options to start with: \"Dashboard Console\" and \"Floor\".\n\n\n**Defining Project Data**\n\nI\'m now defining concise descriptions for the project details. Each project will include before/after image paths, a category, a description of the condition, and key highlights. These include \"Piano-Black Dashboard\" and \"Floor Carpet Extraction\" as starting examples. I\'m focusing on descriptive text based on classic auto detailing processes. Each tab will show an icon, and the slider will reset to 50% when a project is selected.\n\n\n**Expanding Project Definitions**\n\nI\'ve added new project data to the existing list. \"Trunk Pet Hair Eradication\" now includes before/after image paths, category, description, and highlights. Similarly, \"Door Jamb Paint Restoration\" and \"Wheel Brake Dust Purge\" have been fleshed out with detailed information. The new highlights I\'m working on are \"Enzyme soil liquefaction\", \"Rotary fiber lifting agitation\", and \"Deep vacuum extraction wash\". Each now has a category, description, and highlights.\n\n\n"
